  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader, I want the page bar of a list (« ⏮ ‹ Page N › ») to show only when I reach the bottom of the list, so that it does not take space at the top of a list where I almost never change page.\n\nMilestone: **M4**. Source: operator UI comparison of 2026-11-14, capture 04 (Messages, logged in; pseudos and titles redacted).\n\n### Observed (SwiftHFR @ `37c099b5`)\nThe pager (`App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/PagerToolbar.swift`, LOT-185) sits above the tab bar at all times, from the top of the list.\n\n### Why (operator, 2026-11-14)\n- Messages is opened because there are new messages, and they are always at the top: one rarely changes page.\n- The same holds for every topic list: the page change belongs at the end of what one has read.\n- The pager itself is kept (it is the retained SwiftHFR improvement of GAP-024, without the fake total); only when it shows changes.\n\n### Scope\n- **Every paged topic list, Catégories included, and the Messages list** (operator, 2026-11-14): the pager appears when the list is scrolled to its end, and stays hidden above that.\n- A list shorter than the screen shows it at once (its end is visible).\n- VoiceOver: the page actions stay reachable when the bar is hidden (for example as accessibility actions of the list), so that hiding is visual only.\n- Ledger: `gap-edit` of GAP-024 and GAP-221 (glass pager) in the PR's `### Ledger` section.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] At the top of a long list the pager is hidden; at the end it shows; scrolling back up hides it again.\n- [ ] Same behaviour in a category's topic list, Favoris lists that page, search results and Messages.\n- [ ] VoiceOver can change page from anywhere in the list.\n\nRelated: #565 (pager under the tab bar, closed), #649, #865 (top bar title scrolls away), #896 (fifth tab item).\n\n### Operator view (2026-11-14)\n\nThe pager meant here is the bar « ⏮ ‹ Page N › » of the lists (`PagerToolbar.swift`, #881). For the operator it **stays visible at the bottom of the screen at all times**, as it is today after #881. To settle between the operator and ezzz before coding: `status: needs-decision`. If ezzz's « only at the end of the list » is kept, it goes in Réglages › Expérimental (#903) rather than replacing today's behaviour.\n\n### Common ground (operator, 2026-11-14), replacing the « Operator view » above\n\n- While the list scrolls, the pager is **hidden**, which keeps the room ezzz wants.\n- When the list **reaches its end**, the page bubble « ⏮ ‹ Page N › » **appears dynamically** with a short animation, at the bottom of the screen above the tab bar. It hides again when the user scrolls back up.\n- A list shorter than the screen shows it at once, since its end is visible.\n- VoiceOver keeps the page actions reachable at all times (accessibility actions of the list).\n- No setting and no experimental option: this is the default behaviour. ezzz can still object on this issue.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
