   "body": "### Additions (operator, 2026-11-15)\n\nThese go with the page bubble that appears at the end of the list:\n\n1. **Refresh at the bottom too.** When the bubble appears at the end, a refresh button appears next to it. It is the **same** refresh button as the top bar's, reused (one component, one action), not a new one. The top bar keeps its own.\n2. **Tighter spacing between the last row and the bottom controls.** The gap between the last row and the bubble and buttons is too large today. It reads as unused space, like the margin around the floating composer. Reduce it to the system's standard spacing above a floating bar, while keeping the last row fully readable and tappable above the controls (see #852's inset handling).\n3. **Pull up past the end to refresh.** Once the list is at its end, pulling it further up (an overscroll at the bottom) triggers a refresh, like pull-to-refresh at the top.\n   - Show a discreet hint below the last row: « Tirer vers le haut pour actualiser », almost tone on tone (secondary label colour, small).\n   - While refreshing, show the system activity indicator.\n\n### Acceptance criteria (added)\n- [ ] At the end of a list, the bubble and a refresh button appear together. The button runs the same action as the top refresh.\n- [ ] The gap between the last row and the bottom controls is the standard spacing. Measure before and after; screenshots go on the PR.\n- [ ] Pulling up past the end shows the hint, then refreshes on release past the threshold, with a short haptic as at the top. Releasing earlier does nothing.\n- [ ] VoiceOver: refresh is reachable without the gesture, through the button or an accessibility action.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
